This game is a thing where concepts of Interstellar (
) and Moon (
) meet. Except for the finding out what the hell happens there, there's only one typical activity: wandering through various terrains trying not to be causght by the huge radioactive alien thing. Absolute lack of scary moments (the screen just fades to black when things get really fubar).
From what I've figured as early as 2nd chapter start, it is quite clear that main character have met his death by some sort of alien terraforming machine. However the explanation for 'divine resurrection' is postponed till the 6th chapter. The 7th one is an epilogue of a sort, due to all mysteries revealed before.
Is it worth it? As a walking-jumping simulator, maybe. Does it raise any serious moral questions? Well, there are some tiny moments regarding the Creation and Expulsion stories, but nothing that would ignite some serious philosophical activity.
Overall, it tends to be pretty-looking mediocrity of a game.

