The game itself is beautiful, and has a great combat system without tab targeting.
I has nice variety in things you can do with life skills but thats more of a con than a pro, i'll explain at a later part.
The main problems with this game is its a cash-grab, The devs either can't change anything or won't change anything because they dont care and you are forced into pvp at lvl 50+ (and you can't opt out).
Cash-grab;
The game itself sells costumes, pets and a large variety or items in a microtransaction cash shop ingame, this would be fine but these items are more often than not more than 2-3 sometimes even 5x the cost of the initial game. FOR A COSTUME/SKIN. Every single patch they make changes, not that actually effect the game but to change earlygame making more and more players want to stay long enough to put more money into the game.
Dev's not caring;
We've all seen it before Dev making a cool game, and then leaving it behind because they have money (Cube World) and this never works out, in BDO's case it was created in Korea, as a monthly subscription game with cheap cash shop items and active devs and admins helping the playerbase with whatever they wanted, however in these servers (NA/EU) the devs and admins rarely ever do anything, they copy&pasted the game over and simply raised cash shop prices and game expenses to compensate for the monthly subscription fee and didnt change anything. (i'm talking they did events in the same order of the Korean server that came out years before, they even left in the bugs/exploits that were discovered in the Korean server that they simply didnt fix, despite being descovered and fixed already before the patch where said bugs are discovered) You can't get in contact with devs to communicate or get any form of help every single support ticket you submitt is simply a bot compy and pasting you (tested by submitting 10 of the same support ticket, different 'GM' names but same text)
lvl 50+;
You are level 50 and you become pvp enabled, but due to the accuracy system in the game you can't fight anyone above a couple of levels than you without missing 80% of attacks, not to mention their subpar servers making lag a massive factor in pvp, you arent eased into it, you're just thrown into a pool of people insta-killing you all over the place and you can't do anything about it because to even get on their level you need hours of grinding at spots where you're pk'd out of, you need to spend billions of ingame currency to make use of the rng enhancing system (it takes about a week at anywhere under level 60 to get 100mil just to give you a scale) and not to mention the fact that even at the higher levels of the game pvp isnt a fun experience, its you either die in 1 hit or kill in 1 hit and no grey area.
Short summary;
Its a great game but its a monthly subscription game with pay to win features that was copy and pasted, translate and brought to the EU/NA/Russian people and at the start its a great game, but after about 100 hours into the game where you are lvl 56+ with sub-par gear, it pretty much devolved into life skilling (processing, fishing, horse breeding) where you arent even playing the game and are just tabbing into the game once every day for 5 mins.
I have played since the closed beta of the game before it hit steam incase anyone is wondering, according to Raptr, i've got more than 2k hours into the game so i'd like to think i have an idea of what i'm talking about.
P.S. they advertise that they've got new servers to accomodate the steam release, but really they just renamed channels that had the lowest lag and put exp bonuses on them, oh and these channels kick you out and lock you off from them once you hit a certain level or have played for a certain time so you'll be stuck in the laggy ones too.

A mixture of JRPG and fairy tales, Child of Light shows the same poetry as The Last Night of the Rabbit by Telltale, with many bonuses.
Pros:
+ Beautiful graphics;
+ A pleasant twist on the classical JRPG and platform games;
+ Two-players allowed: play it with your partner (seriously, too many games ignore this feature)!
+ Rhymes and lore in verses, which add to the magic;
+ Combat and crafting systems are both simple for the basics (so you don't have to look for advice online) and challenging (awesome to plan strategies even if you're not the thinking type).
Cons:
- The plot is rather linear, with no multiple ending (which would have been good);
- As a consequence, low replayability.
- Oculi farming is, all in all, a waste of time: it's hard to come up with a specific, maximized oculi set.
